cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this reproduction study or its harness, cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Parity holonomy in Boolean constraint networks: a reproduction study of five claims, one refutation, and a checksum that is not a memory"
abstract: >-
  An independent reproduction of the five verdicts published by the kostyk348/paradox-logic
  repository: paradox as Mermin/GHZ contextuality, defect thermodynamics, topological parity
  memory, novelty as a change of topological class, and the cohomological diagonal lemma. Six
  experiments are re-run from a pinned commit and compared byte for byte against the result files
  committed with the code; four verdicts are checked against numbers, and the parity invariant is
  sharpened into a measurable statement about minimum distance.
authors:
  - family-names: Parashchuk
    given-names: Konstantin
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Saint Petersburg, Russia"
    website: "https://github.com/kostyk348"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - parity holonomy
  - contextuality
  - Boolean constraint networks
  - error detecting codes
  - frustration
  - reproducibility
